{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_002: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200 → Acc 0.520), so the most critical uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit over the RNA-only baseline. config_051 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) keeps the RNA encoder and profile setting identical to config_002 and introduces only the image modality with a simple concat fusion, thereby isolating the effect of adding image information. This is the cleanest possible A/B comparison: any performance difference directly attributes to the image channel rather than confounds from a different encoder, profile setting, or aggregation scheme. Under a limited budget, establishing whether multimodality helps at all is the highest-value information to obtain before investing in more complex multiprofile or aggregation variants."
}

